  README.md:393:## 10. Development narrative
  README.md:394:
> README.md:395:The build log with full decision history is `<SCRATCHPAD>/BUILD.md`. In brief:
  README.md:396:
  README.md:397:**What changed along the way.** The taxonomy was **reshaped from 12 classes to 10**
> README.md:398:mid-build: `oos_business_tax` and `oos_other_agency` were merged (they shared a bucket
  README.md:399:*and* an action, so the split bought nothing downstream, and the classifier could not
  README.md:400:separate them — one scored F1 0.000 with half its errors landing on its sibling), and
  README.md:401:`account_specific` was **demoted from a class to a flag**. That second change is the
> README.md:402:more interesting one: being about your own record is a property an enquiry *has*, not
  README.md:403:a topic it is *about* — "how do instalments work" and "what is the status of my
  README.md:404:instalment plan" differ by one possessive. Topical vocabulary dominated the one or two
  README.md:405:tokens carrying the actual signal, so as a class it failed; as a lexical flag consulted
  README.md:406:before any confidence, it works.
  README.md:421:
  README.md:422:**Things that broke and what they taught.** Two free-tier models were *withdrawn*
> README.md:423:mid-build — Groq's `llama-3.3-70b` and Gemini's `gemini-2.0-flash`, both returning 404.
  README.md:424:They failed differently, and that contrast shaped the design: the Groq withdrawal was
> README.md:425:silent (dropped samples fell back to a uniform distribution, so numbers were quietly
  README.md:426:wrong), while the Gemini one was loud (drafting has an explicit failure path, so items
  README.md:427:escalated with their SOPs and the error was recorded on the state). That is why the
  README.md:428:model identifier is stamped into every result file and why the drafter has **no
  README.md:429:template fallback** that would mask an outage.
  README.md:432:DistilBERT on deployment size. Gemini for drafting and Groq for judging, chosen from
  README.md:433:different families so no model is scored on its own output. GPT-4o for generation
> README.md:434:only — build-time and paid, with its output frozen and committed so no grader re-runs
  README.md:435:a paid step.
  README.md:436:
  README.md:437:---
  README.md:438:
  README.md:439:## 11. Coding agent usage
  README.md:440:
> README.md:441:This project was built with **Claude Code** (Claude Opus) as a pair-programming and
  README.md:442:audit partner, used in three distinct modes:
  README.md:443:
  README.md:444:1. **Implementation.** Most module code and tests were drafted with the agent against
> README.md:445:   a design I specified in `BUILD.md`, then reviewed and corrected by me.
