  README.md:438:
  README.md:439:## 11. Coding agent usage
  README.md:440:
> README.md:441:This project was built with **Claude Code** (Claude Opus) as a pair-programming and
  README.md:442:audit partner, used in three distinct modes:
  README.md:443:
  README.md:444:1. **Implementation.** Most module code and tests were drafted with the agent against
> README.md:445:   a design I specified in `BUILD.md`, then reviewed and corrected by me.
  README.md:446:2. **Adversarial audit.** The agent was asked to attack its own output — probing
  README.md:447:   invariants exhaustively rather than reading them. This is where the highest-value
  README.md:448:   findings came from, each reproduced at the command line before being fixed:
  README.md:449:
  README.md:465:   the command line before being written down.
  README.md:466:
> README.md:467:Where the agent and I disagreed, the disagreement is recorded in `BUILD.md` rather than
  README.md:468:silently resolved — including one case where I asked it to broaden PII detection and
  README.md:469:the measurement showed the change would damage classifier input for no real gain.
  README.md:470:
  README.md:471:**Session logs** are in `AI assistant logs/`.
  README.md:483:  more than doubling the variants of the existing ones, and would widen the calibration
  README.md:484:  split — currently the binding constraint on the temperature fit.
> README.md:485:- Real anonymised enquiries as a validation-only slice, to test whether the synthetic
  README.md:486:  situation set resembles the real distribution — the one thing this project cannot
